{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_bdrk_2vuqgqc2ealwdeadk5muqmdjguscsdjc2nqfn3y543ena7qd77xa","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"So the version script explicitly localizes everything except listed names. The `local: *` is the culprit - it forces _init/_fini to be local. We need to either:\n1. Use a linker wrapper that overrides this script\n2. Use `-fuse-ld` with an alternative linker\n\nLooking more carefully — when ld processes multiple version scripts via `--version-script` and `--dynamic-list`, the rules combine. But `local: *` will localize anything not in `global:`, regardless of `--dynamic-list`.\n\nLet me write a custom linker wrapper that strips the local rule and replaces it:\n\nActually, the simplest approach — use a linker wrapper that overrides the version-script:"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":315,"cache_read_input_tokens":65894,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":315,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"8fa2b476-2198-4c70-95af-708e3b870d4c","uuid":"73b9e2bc-7c47-4905-a02e-e38bc64e15b8"}
